  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the given circuit the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is:</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0092_f0cf1a5657f2.png\" style=\"width: 362px; height: 250px;\" />&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0092_707380db0047.png\" style=\"width: 351px; height: 260px;\" /></p><p>Potential distribution at each point in the circuit is shown in above diagram.</p><p>Since, both&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;resistors&nbsp;are maintained at same potential difference, so current will be same, thus, using Ohm&#39;s law,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>Now, current&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>Hence, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
}